// src/std/mem/mem.zen
// The folder's public surface: starred re-exports only, so submodules
// can move a declaration between mem_alloc/mem_arena/mem_ptr freely.
//
// The law this folder carries: there is NO ambient allocator —
// anything that needs memory takes an Alloc.
//
// Absent names are module-private on purpose: ArenaState (what an
// arena is made of isn't part of what it is), PAGE_BYTES, HEADER_BYTES,
// align_up.

// the interface and its one failure: everything that allocates takes
// an Alloc, one way to run out of memory
AllocError*, Alloc* = std.mem.mem_alloc

// the implementation owning the memory, and the page authority it
// draws from. Arena is Drop; the Alloc handle onto it is not. Page
// appears because Mem's signature names it (law 6, no exemptions)
Arena*, Mem*, Page* = std.mem.mem_arena

// the raw floor. Zen has no pointer sigil, so a raw pointer is
// Ptr<T>; a collection owning nothing holds null_ptr<T>()
Ptr*, null_ptr* = std.mem.mem_ptr
